\DOC ENSURES_EVENTS_WHILE_UP2_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_EVENTS_WHILE_UP2_TAC : term -> term -> term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Reduces an {ensures} goal about a program containing a counted loop to a single
conjunctive goal made up of a non-triviality condition on the iteration count,
an entry step, a parametrised loop-body step, and an exit step.

\DESCRIBE
The arguments are {k : term}, the loop trip count (a numeral or an arithmetic
term); {pc1 : term}, the program address at the loop head, used as the target
of the entry step, as the start of the body, and as the body's next address
while more iterations remain; {pc2 : term}, the address reached after the final
iteration, used as the body's next address on the last iteration and as the
start of the exit step; and {loop_inv : term}, a function {\i s. ...} giving
the loop invariant on the state at iteration index {i}, which is inserted into
the intermediate pre/postconditions. The assumptions {A} are left untouched and
the conclusion is replaced by a conjunction of four parts: {~(k = 0)}; an
{ensures} from the original precondition to an intermediate state description
built from {pc1}, {loop_inv} instantiated at {0}, and the original
postcondition's event component indexed at {0}; a universally quantified body
obligation {forall i. i < k /\ ~(i = k) /\ ~(k = 0) /\ 0 < k ==> ensures ...},
whose precondition uses index {i} at {pc1} and whose postcondition uses index
{i + 1} at the address {if i + 1 < k then pc1 else pc2}; and an {ensures} from
the state at index {k} at {pc2} to the original postcondition. The frame
({MAYCHANGE ...} component) of the original goal is reused unchanged in each
{ensures}, and the loaded-program condition from the precondition is propagated
into the intermediate state descriptions.
{
   A ?- ensures ...
   ========================================================= ENSURES_EVENTS_WHILE_UP2_TAC k pc1 pc2 loop_inv
   A ?- ~(k = 0) /\
        ensures ... /\
        (forall i. i < k /\ ~(i = k) /\ ~(k = 0) /\ 0 < k ==> ensures ...) /\
        ensures ...
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this transformation occurs, always on {ensures}
goals of this shape.

\ENDDOC
